## Context

Child of tracker 0029. The Multilingual Menagerie's representative core has to
match a real library, and until now nothing said which one or how
(`conception/0029-golden-fixture-structure-review.md` §3, the author's own
proposal: "derive library size, item-type distribution, attachment file-type
distribution, attachments-per-item distribution from the author's existing
real library; record the sampling method and comparison so the fixture can
claim representativeness"). This ticket builds that sampling frame: a
read-only census of the author's Zotero library over the local API, producing
the marginal distributions a quota sample of documents must reproduce.

The fixture perimeter follows the 2026-08-31 ruling: what Zotero shows, so the
group library is in and the trash and feeds are out. The census counts all
three, and reports the last two apart so the exclusion is a measured one.

## Relevant files

- `bench/library_census.py` — the probe: local API listing, full-text
  counters from the control plugin (`bench/zotero-fulltext-plugin/`) with the
  API's `/fulltext` route as fallback, an immutable SQLite read for the two
  marginals the API does not expose (annotations by type, feed libraries)
- `tests/test_library_census.py` — fixture API of known composition; the
  read-only proof (source, monkeypatched transport, and a real HTTP server
  recording methods); the aggregate-only proof (no key, title, file name or
  note text in the artifact)
- `bench/results/0029-library-census/census.json` — the committed artifact
- `verification/LIBRARY-CENSUS-0029.md` — method, provenance, the marginals
  as tables, and what they imply for the representative core
- `bench/check_figures.py` — every figure the report quotes, declared

## Privacy and safety

The artifact carries counts and quantiles only. Every request is a GET; the
SQLite handle is `mode=ro&immutable=1`. Both properties are asserted by tests,
including one against a real server that records the methods it saw.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `bench/library_census.py` runs against Zotero 10 with `--base-url`,
      `--output`, `--include-group`, `--sqlite`; no hardcoded paths
- [ ] `tests/test_library_census.py` in the fast tier proves the counts on a
      known fixture and proves the tool never issues a write
- [ ] the real census committed under `bench/results/0029-library-census/`
      with host, date, Zotero version in its provenance
- [ ] `verification/LIBRARY-CENSUS-0029.md` reports the marginals and reads
      them for the representative core: which cells are large, which are
      rare but present, which the API cannot measure
- [ ] the child row and a log line on tracker 0029
- [ ] `make check` green
